{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q10859784","formula":"C₁₃H₂₁NO₂","hill":"C13H21NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"IRIS"},"descriptions":{"en":"Iris, also known as 2-methoxy-5-ethoxy-4-methylamphetamine or as DOM-5ETO, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine, amphetamine, and DOx families related to DOM. It is derivative of DOM in which the methoxy group at the 5 position has been replaced with an ethoxy group. In his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved), Alexander Shulgin lists Iris's dose as greater than 9 mg orally and its duration as unknown. The effects of Iris at tested doses included possible threshold effects and lightheadedness."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":44719575,"mass":223.31,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOC1=CC(=C(C=C1C)OC)CC(C)N","inchikey":"IPJRCKIREPMKNE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(5-ethoxy-2-methoxy-4-methylphenyl)propan-2-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44719575","atoms":37,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.714,"y":-0.669,"z":-0.544,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.077,"y":2.005,"z":0.018,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.626,"y":-2.641,"z":-0.283,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.164,"y":-0.739,"z":-0.805,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.378,"y":-1.971,"z":0.094,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.878,"y":0.0,"z":-0.521,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.897,"y":1.337,"z":-0.123,"el":"C"},{"x":0.338,"y":-0.669,"z":-0.661,"el":"C"},{"x":1.535,"y":-0.001,"z":-0.403,"el":"C"},{"x":1.516,"y":1.336,"z":-0.005,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.455,"y":-1.608,"z":1.577,"el":"C"},{"x":0.3,"y":2.005,"z":0.135,"el":"C"},{"x":2.788,"y":2.066,"z":0.276,"el":"C"},{"x":2.905,"y":-1.824,"z":0.27,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.004,"y":3.369,"z":0.429,"el":"C"},{"x":4.384,"y":-1.995,"z":0.544,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.14,"y":-1.049,"z":-1.859,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.03,"y":-0.072,"z":-0.716,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.56